cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "GenIce3: Hydrogen-Disordered Ice Generator"
abstract: >-
  GenIce3 is the current GenIce. It builds hydrogen-disordered ice and clathrate
  hydrate structures for molecular simulation. From a catalogue of unit cells
  it assembles supercells
  whose hydrogen-bond network satisfies the Bernal-Fowler ice rules and whose
  net polarization is driven toward a prescribed target, fills clathrate cages
  with guests, substitutes ions and protonic or Bjerrum defects, and writes the
  result in the formats of common simulation and visualization programs.
